   "section": "Abstract",
   "page": 1,
   "source": "We present a microfluidic platform for rapid detection of lead ions in drinking water. The sensor achieves a limit of detection of 0.8 µg/L within 12 min, which is lower than the WHO guideline of 10 µg/L [1]. Unlike previous colorimetric assays, our method does not require sample pretreatment and remains stable at 4 °C for 30 days (Fig. 1). These results suggest that the platform may be suitable for field deployment in resource-limited settings.",
   "translation": "我们提出了一种用于快速检测饮用水中铅离子的微流控平台。该传感器在 12 min 内达到 0.8 µg/L 的检出限，低于世界卫生组织（WHO）10 µg/L 的指导值 [1]。与以往的比色法不同，本方法无需样品前处理，并在 4 °C 下 30 天内保持稳定（图 1）。这些结果表明，该平台可能适用于资源有限场景下的现场部署。",
